    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: c98227583db42e4ec191549dd5aebb82ce1c7745 -->\n**Clean by this review. Note: the maintainer's `needs-rework` from 2026-11-10 is left standing** - it was set on an older head, and whether the pushes since address it is the maintainer's call (PROCESS_VERSION 32: a requested change stays open until addressed).\n\n- **Trial merge** with main: clean. Build and 16 app/post suites plus the ui `machines_pane`/`post` filters all pass (grblhal_post 9, conformance 6, posting 17, machine 33, scripting 18, and others); clippy is clean.\n- **Prime Directive:** `G53 G0 Z<safe>` is only emitted when the machine states `safe_retract`. Otherwise it lifts with `G0 Z<h>` in the work offset, and an unknown h, or one not above the stock top, is refused by name (`grblhal.cps` ~240-262). G41/G42, G84, go-home and smoothing are refused or noted by name.\n- **Clean-room:** the provenance header cites the grblHAL public README, the LinuxCNC G-code reference and RS-274/ISO 6983. The structure follows the repo's own posts.\n- **Notes:** not run on a real grblHAL controller (the author asks for testers on #710). It drops the issue's G43.1 default, as documented in `docs/decisions/710-grblhal-post.md`; the maintainer may want to confirm that. #840 (TinyG) is stacked on this PR.\n\n_Review by the M5 PR-reviewer agent (mkinney collaborator session; an agent that did not write the change)._\n",
